## Why This Is Asked
This question probes understanding of per-tenant isolation, backpressure, and queueing strategies under load, a common real-world challenge in llm-ops gateways.

## Key Concepts
- Priority queues and scheduling (WFQ, weighted RR)
- Backpressure and saturation handling
- Tenant isolation and SLA guarantees
- Observability: latency, tail latency, fairness

## Code Example
```javascript
class Scheduler {
  constructor() {
    this.queues = {Gold: [], Silver: [], Bronze: []};
  }
  enqueue(tenant, priority, job) {
    this.queues[priority].push({tenant, job});
  }
  dequeue() {
    for (const p of ['Gold','Silver','Bronze']) {
      if (this.queues[p].length) return this.queues[p].shift();
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and ensure Gold latency bounds under burst?
- How would you adapt weights if Bronze saturates frequently?

